# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Arca — environment
# Copy to `.env.local`. Every value here is optional: with none of them set the
# app boots against the in-memory fixture repository, which is how you develop
# the UI without a database. See src/db/repository.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL. Set this and the app switches from fixtures to the real
# object-graph schema. Vercel Postgres and Neon both hand you this string.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/arca?sslmode=require"

# Auth.js / Discord OAuth — SCOPE.md §4, M1.
#
# Set ALL THREE and the app switches from the member picker to real Discord
# sign-in. Set none and the picker stays, which is what lets `npm run dev` work
# with no database and no Discord application.
#
# Membership is NOT granted by signing in: a Discord account reaches the app
# only if `users.discord_id` matches a row that is a member of this campaign.
# Anyone else gets the "not at this table" screen, which shows them the id to
# hand the GM. Linking is one statement:
#
#   UPDATE users SET discord_id = '<their id>' WHERE display_name = 'Kova';
#
# Because membership lives in the database, Discord sign-in requires
# DATABASE_URL — with fixtures there is nothing to link against.
#
# AUTH_SECRET=""            # openssl rand -base64 32
# AUTH_DISCORD_ID=""
# AUTH_DISCORD_SECRET=""

# The campaign this deployment serves. One campaign per deployment for now
# (SCOPE.md §13 Q5).
# ARCA_CAMPAIGN_ID="00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
